@*
    REQ-UI-050 — the Playbook axis of /effort ("Phase efficiency"), built to
    docs/mockups/effort-playbook.html and to the "Playbook state" component map in
    docs/TfLens-UIDesign.md §Screen: Phase effort.

    Four rules this surface exists to hold, and everything else here is in service of them:

      * BRD-163 — a harness with no normalized producer renders
        "Phase effort telemetry unsupported for this harness". That is a DATA GAP, which is a different
        fact from a harness that ran and spent nothing, so it is never a zero and never an empty
        measured figure. On today's data this is the state the screen is actually in.
      * BRD-156 / ADR-027 — wall-clock elapsed, observed active time and human effort are three
        separate concepts. `assistant_elapsed_ms` and `tool_elapsed_ms` legitimately overlap and are
        never added; `coverage: partial` renders as an explicit lower bound; `unavailable` renders as
        no figure at all.
      * BRD-159 — fan-out is `contributors / spawned`. A grandchild renders beneath its parent and is
        counted exactly once, child usage is already inside the phase totals and is never summed onto
        them again, and `spawned − contributors` is a zero-token or non-contributing child, never an
        inferred failure. An absent child agent type shows unavailable, never guessed.
      * BRD-160 — measured provider dollars and a tokens-times-rate-card figure live on separate cards
        and never share a series, a total or an aggregate. A `zero-unverified` cost carries its status
        and its caveat, never "free" and never a measured $0.

    Every figure arrives from IPlaybookReportBuilder.BuildPhaseReportAsync as a PhaseValue, which
    structurally refuses to be a number when nothing eligible supported it — the same technique as
    Figure/FigureText on the TechieFlow axis. No cohort rule is re-implemented here: the four nested
    cohorts and their exclusion counts are the engine's, and this file only renders them.

    REQ-NFR-023 (BRD-169) note: no rate-card dollar is computed on this surface at all. The report
    type deliberately carries no estimate member, so the estimate card states its absence rather than
    manufacturing a number that would read as spend.
*@
@using System.Globalization
@using TfLens.Core.Playbook
@using TfLens.Core.Repos
@using TrBlazeUI.Components.Empty
@inject IPlaybookReportBuilder objReportBuilder
@inject IRepoListReader objRepoListReader

<div class="pb-effort">

    @if (!objIsLoaded)
    {
        <Card>
            <CardContent Class="p-6">
                <div class="flex flex-col gap-3">
                    <Skeleton Class="h-4 w-full" />
                    <Skeleton Class="h-4 w-3/4" />
                    <Skeleton Class="h-4 w-1/2" />
                </div>
            </CardContent>
        </Card>
    }
    else if (objLoadError is not null)
    {
        <Alert Variant="AlertVariant.Danger" data-testid="pb-effort-error">
            <LucideIcon Name="triangle-alert" Size="18" />
            <AlertTitle>Couldn't read the phase-effort report</AlertTitle>
            <AlertDescription>@objLoadError</AlertDescription>
        </Alert>
    }
    else if (objReport is { } vReport)
    {
        @* REQ-UI-050 — the filters render on every state, because the repository select is the one
           control that re-queries the engine and so is how a reader reaches a supported repository
           from an unsupported one. *@
        <Card data-testid="pb-effort-filters">
            <CardContent Class="p-4">
                <div class="pb-filters">
                    <span class="pb-filters-label">
                        <LucideIcon Name="filter" Size="16" />
                        Filters
                    </span>

                    @foreach (var vFilter in Filters)
                    {
                        <span class="pb-filter">
                            @* TR-020 — SelectValue renders the raw bound value until SelectContent has
                               rendered once, so the closed trigger needs DisplayTextSelector. *@
                            <Select TValue="string"
                                    Value="@vFilter.Value"
                                    ValueChanged="@(aValue => OnFilterChangedAsync(vFilter.Key, aValue))"
                                    DisplayTextSelector="@(aValue => vFilter.LabelOf(aValue))">
                                <SelectTrigger data-testid="@($"pb-effort-filter-{vFilter.Key}")">
                                    <SelectValue Placeholder="@vFilter.Options[0].Label" />
                                </SelectTrigger>
                                <SelectContent>
                                    @foreach (var vOption in vFilter.Options)
                                    {
                                        <SelectItem TValue="string" Value="@vOption.Key" Text="@vOption.Label">
                                            @vOption.Label
                                        </SelectItem>
                                    }
                                </SelectContent>
                            </Select>
                        </span>
                    }

                    <span class="pb-filters-spacer"></span>
                    <Button Variant="ButtonVariant.Ghost"
                            Size="ButtonSize.Small"
                            OnClick="ResetFiltersAsync"
                            data-testid="pb-effort-filter-reset">Reset</Button>
                </div>

                <p class="pb-note" data-testid="pb-effort-filter-scope">
                    @FilterScopeNote
                </p>
            </CardContent>
        </Card>

        @if (!vReport.Harness.IsSupported)
        {
            @* BRD-163 — the whole numeric body is withheld here on purpose. Rendering the tiles with
               their cohorts at zero would state "this harness ran and spent nothing" while measuring
               "no adapter emits the normalized schema", which are different facts. *@
            <Alert Variant="AlertVariant.Warning" AccentBorder="true" data-testid="pb-effort-unsupported">
                <LucideIcon Name="triangle-alert" Size="18" />
                <AlertTitle>
                    @PlaybookPhaseVocabulary.UnsupportedHarnessMessage — <span class="font-mono">@HarnessName</span>
                </AlertTitle>
                <AlertDescription>
                    No adapter for this harness emits the normalized schema-2 phase record yet, so there
                    is nothing to render for its phase executions on this axis. This is a data gap, which
                    is a different fact from a harness that ran and spent nothing: it is never rendered as
                    0 and never as an empty measured figure. The harnesses that do emit the record are
                    @NormalizedHarnessList.
                </AlertDescription>
            </Alert>
        }
        else if (vReport.Executions.Count == 0)
        {
            <Empty Title="No phase-metric bundle imported yet"
                   Description="@NoBundleDescription"
                   data-testid="pb-effort-empty">
                <Icon>
                    <LucideIcon Name="gauge" Size="32" />
                </Icon>
            </Empty>
        }
        else
        {
            @* ---------------------------------------------------------------- SUMMARY (BRD-161) *@
            @* Eight tiles, each carrying its own `n of N eligible` beneath it. The counts travel with
               the figure rather than sitting in a page footer, because a reader who can see a number
               must be able to see what it was computed over without looking anywhere else. *@
            <StatGroup Columns="4" data-testid="pb-effort-summary">

                <StatTile Title="Completed phases"
                          IconName="circle-check"
                          Accent="StatAccent.Chart1"
                          Value="@vReport.Quality.Completed.ToString("N0", CultureInfo.InvariantCulture)"
                          Description="@CompletedCaption"
                          data-testid="pb-effort-tile-completed" />

                <StatTile Title="Wall clock — median / p90"
                          IconName="clock"
                          Accent="StatAccent.Chart5"
                          Description="@CaptionOf(vReport.ElapsedMsMedian)"
                          data-testid="pb-effort-tile-wallclock">
                    <ValueContent>
                        <span class="pb-value-pair">
                            <PhaseValueText Value="@vReport.ElapsedMsMedian.Value"
                                            MeasuredText="@DurationOf(vReport.ElapsedMsMedian.Value)"
                                            TestId="pb-effort-elapsed-median" />
                            <span class="pb-value-second">
                                / <PhaseValueText Value="@vReport.ElapsedMsP90.Value"
                                                  MeasuredText="@DurationOf(vReport.ElapsedMsP90.Value)"
                                                  TestId="pb-effort-elapsed-p90" />
                            </span>
                        </span>
                    </ValueContent>
                </StatTile>

                <StatTile Title="@PlaybookPhaseVocabulary.ObservedActiveLabel"
                          IconName="activity"
                          Accent="StatAccent.Chart2"
                          Description="@CaptionOf(vReport.ObservedActiveMsTotal)"
                          data-testid="pb-effort-tile-active">
                    <ValueContent>
                        <PhaseValueText Value="@vReport.ObservedActiveMsTotal.Value"
                                        MeasuredText="@DurationOf(vReport.ObservedActiveMsTotal.Value)"
                                        TestId="pb-effort-active" />
                    </ValueContent>
                </StatTile>

                <StatTile Title="Sub-agents — contributors / spawned"
                          IconName="git-fork"
                          Accent="StatAccent.Chart3"
                          Value="@FanoutHeadline"
                          Description="@FanoutCaption"
                          data-testid="pb-effort-tile-fanout" />

                <StatTile Title="Token components"
                          IconName="database"
                          Accent="StatAccent.Chart1"
                          Description="@TokenCaption"
                          data-testid="pb-effort-tile-tokens">
                    <ValueContent>
                        <PhaseValueText Value="@vReport.Tokens.Output" TestId="pb-effort-tokens-output" />
                    </ValueContent>
                </StatTile>

                @* BRD-160 — the ONE tile carrying dollars, and they are the provider's own. *@
                <StatTile Title="Measured provider cost"
                          IconName="dollar-sign"
                          Accent="StatAccent.Chart2"
                          Description="@MeasuredCostCaption"
                          data-testid="pb-cost-measured">
                    <TitleAdornment>
                        <Badge Variant="BadgeVariant.Secondary">measured</Badge>
                    </TitleAdornment>
                    <ValueContent>
                        <span class="@(vReport.MeasuredCostUsd.Usd is null ? "pb-refused" : null)"
                              data-testid="pb-cost-measured-value">@MeasuredCostText</span>
                    </ValueContent>
                </StatTile>

                <StatTile Title="Incomplete windows"
                          IconName="triangle-alert"
                          Accent="StatAccent.Chart4"
                          Value="@vReport.Quality.Incomplete.ToString("N0", CultureInfo.InvariantCulture)"
                          Description="@IncompleteCaption"
                          data-testid="pb-effort-tile-incomplete" />

                <StatTile Title="Quarantined"
                          IconName="x"
                          Accent="StatAccent.Destructive"
                          Value="@vReport.Quality.Quarantined.ToString("N0", CultureInfo.InvariantCulture)"
                          Description="@QuarantineCaption"
                          data-testid="pb-effort-tile-quarantined" />
            </StatGroup>

            @* BRD-160 — its own card, its own row, its own dashed styling. Nothing on it shares a
               series, a total or an aggregate with the measured tile above. *@
            <Card data-testid="pb-cost-estimate">
                <CardContent Class="p-4">
                    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-start gap-3">
                        <span class="tflens-stat-chip tflens-accent-4 shrink-0">
                            <LucideIcon Name="dollar-sign" Size="16" />
                        </span>
                        <div class="min-w-0 flex flex-col gap-1">
                            <span class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2">
                                <CardTitle Class="text-base">Rate-card estimate</CardTitle>
                                <Badge Variant="BadgeVariant.Outline"
                                       data-testid="pb-cost-estimate-label">estimate — tokens × rate card</Badge>
                                <span class="pb-refused" data-testid="pb-cost-estimate-value">
                                    @PlaybookPhaseVocabulary.Unavailable
                                </span>
                            </span>
                            <CardDescription>
                                No priced figure is produced on this axis. A tokens-times-rate-card dollar
                                is an operator-editable input, not spend — nobody was billed it — so it is
                                never placed on an effort tile and never added to, subtracted from or
                                charted beside the measured provider cost, whose cohort is smaller and
                                different. Estimates live on Routing &amp; economics, on a card of their own.
                            </CardDescription>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </CardContent>
            </Card>

            @* BRD-156 / ADR-027 — the three timing concepts, stated where the timing figures are read. *@
            <Alert Variant="AlertVariant.Warning" data-testid="pb-effort-timing-note">
                <LucideIcon Name="triangle-alert" Size="18" />
                <AlertTitle>Three timing concepts, and they never substitute for one another</AlertTitle>
                <AlertDescription>
                    Wall-clock elapsed is how long the command window stayed open. Observed active time is
                    the producer's union of assistant and tool intervals across main and child sessions,
                    with overlapping and nested work counted once — <span class="font-mono">assistant_elapsed_ms</span>
                    and <span class="font-mono">tool_elapsed_ms</span> legitimately overlap and are never
                    added together. Human effort is never captured and never inferred. Active time is busy
                    wall time; it is not human effort, not CPU time, not utilization and not additive compute.
                </AlertDescription>
            </Alert>

            @* ---------------------------------------------------------------------- CHARTS *@
            <div class="pb-section-head">
                <h3 class="pb-h3">Trends</h3>
                <span class="text-sm text-muted-foreground">
                    Read these as a description of what ran, not as a ranking of phases — a command that
                    costs more than another is a fact about what that command is.
                </span>
            </div>

            @* TR-028 — BarChart exposes no axis, grid or data-label control and no route to
               ApexChartOptions, and ChartContainer paints a card of its own inside the card a chart
               already sits in. The approved design draws segmented bars with the value printed above
               each one and no axis at all, so these are the mockup's own CSS bars rather than a chart
               component fought into shape; every segment is also printed as text in the tables below,
               so nothing here is readable only as a picture. *@
            <div class="pb-grid-2" data-testid="pb-effort-charts">

                <Card Class="h-full" data-testid="pb-chart-tokens">
                    <CardHeader>
                        <div class="flex flex-wrap items-start justify-between gap-2">
                            <span class="flex min-w-0 flex-col gap-1">
                                <CardTitle Class="text-base">Tokens by command phase</CardTitle>
                                <CardDescription>
                                    Stacked into the five token legs · valid rows with
                                    <span class="font-mono">token_status: complete</span>
                                </CardDescription>
                            </span>
                            <Badge Variant="BadgeVariant.Outline">@PhaseCommandGroup.DimensionLabel</Badge>
                        </div>
                    </CardHeader>
                    <CardContent Class="pt-0">
                        @if (TokenBars.Count > 0)
                        {
                            <div class="pb-bars">
                                @foreach (var vBar in TokenBars)
                                {
                                    <span class="pb-bar">
                                        <span class="pb-bar-value">@TokenText(vBar.Total)</span>
                                        <span class="pb-bar-stack" style="@BarHeightCss(vBar.Total, TokenBarMax)">
                                            @foreach (var vLeg in vBar.Legs)
                                            {
                                                <i class="@vLeg.CssClass"
                                                   style="@LegHeightCss(vLeg.Tokens, vBar.Total)"
                                                   title="@($"{vLeg.Label}: {vLeg.Tokens:N0}")"></i>
                                            }
                                        </span>
                                        <span class="pb-bar-label font-mono">@vBar.CommandPhase</span>
                                    </span>
                                }
                            </div>
                            <div class="pb-legend">
                                @foreach (var vLeg in LegendLegs)
                                {
                                    <span class="pb-legend-item">
                                        <i class="@vLeg.CssClass"></i>
                                        <span class="font-mono">@vLeg.Label</span>
                                    </span>
                                }
                            </div>
                        }
                        else
                        {
                            <p class="pb-refused" data-testid="pb-chart-tokens-empty">
                                No window has a complete token status yet, so there is no series to draw.
                            </p>
                        }
                    </CardContent>
                </Card>

                <Card Class="h-full" data-testid="pb-chart-duration">
                    <CardHeader>
                        <div class="flex flex-wrap items-start justify-between gap-2">
                            <span class="flex min-w-0 flex-col gap-1">
                                <CardTitle Class="text-base">Duration distribution</CardTitle>
                                <CardDescription>Complete windows only</CardDescription>
                            </span>
                            <Badge Variant="BadgeVariant.Outline" data-testid="pb-chart-duration-excluded">
                                @vReport.Quality.Incomplete incomplete excluded
                            </Badge>
                        </div>
                    </CardHeader>
                    <CardContent Class="pt-0">
                        <div class="pb-bars">
                            @foreach (var vBucket in DurationBuckets)
                            {
                                <span class="pb-bar">
                                    <span class="pb-bar-value">@vBucket.Count</span>
                                    <span class="pb-bar-stack" style="@BarHeightCss(vBucket.Count, DurationBucketMax)">
                                        <i class="pb-leg-5" style="height:100%"></i>
                                    </span>
                                    <span class="pb-bar-label">@vBucket.Label</span>
                                </span>
                            }
                        </div>
                        <p class="pb-note">
                            The excluded count is on the card face. An <span class="font-mono">eof</span>
                            window has no end timestamp and no elapsed time — it is not a fast run, and
                            dropping it silently would make this distribution look tighter than it is.
                        </p>
                    </CardContent>
                </Card>

                @* BRD-159 — fan-out as contributors / spawned, with the difference named for what it is. *@
                <Card Class="h-full" data-testid="pb-chart-fanout">
                    <CardHeader>
                        <div class="flex flex-wrap items-start justify-between gap-2">
                            <span class="flex min-w-0 flex-col gap-1">
                                <CardTitle Class="text-base">Sub-agent fan-out</CardTitle>
                                <CardDescription>
                                    Windows whose <span class="font-mono">tokens_scope</span> could have
                                    seen a child; the rest never read the transcripts and are excluded
                                    rather than counted as a zero
                                </CardDescription>
                            </span>
                            <Badge Variant="BadgeVariant.Outline">contributors / spawned</Badge>
                        </div>
                    </CardHeader>
                    <CardContent Class="pt-0">
                        <div class="pb-bars">
                            @foreach (var vBar in FanoutBars)
                            {
                                <span class="pb-bar">
                                    <span class="pb-bar-value">@vBar.Text</span>
                                    <span class="pb-bar-stack" style="@BarHeightCss(vBar.Count, FanoutBarMax)">
                                        <i class="@vBar.CssClass" style="height:100%"></i>
                                    </span>
                                    <span class="pb-bar-label">@vBar.Label</span>
                                </span>
                            }
                        </div>
                        <p class="pb-note" data-testid="pb-fanout-note">@FanoutNote</p>
                    </CardContent>
                </Card>

                @* BRD-160 — dollars and tokens on one card, and every dollar on it is measured. There is
                   no estimated series here to separate them from, because none is computed on this axis. *@
                <Card Class="h-full" data-testid="pb-chart-cost">
                    <CardHeader>
                        <div class="flex flex-wrap items-start justify-between gap-2">
                            <span class="flex min-w-0 flex-col gap-1">
                                <CardTitle Class="text-base">Measured cost and tokens by model</CardTitle>
                                <CardDescription>
                                    Provider-reported dollars only, over the executions whose
                                    <span class="font-mono">cost_status</span> was complete on every
                                    contributing model
                                </CardDescription>
                            </span>
                            <Badge Variant="BadgeVariant.Secondary">measured, never estimated</Badge>
                        </div>
                    </CardHeader>
                    <CardContent Class="pt-0">
                        @if (CostBars.Count > 0)
                        {
                            <div class="pb-bars">
                                @foreach (var vBar in CostBars)
                                {
                                    <span class="pb-bar">
                                        <span class="pb-bar-value">@vBar.Text</span>
                                        <span class="pb-bar-stack" style="@BarHeightCss(vBar.Amount, CostBarMax)">
                                            <i class="pb-leg-2" style="height:100%"></i>
                                        </span>
                                        <span class="pb-bar-label font-mono">@vBar.Model</span>
                                    </span>
                                }
                            </div>
                        }
                        else
                        {
                            <p class="pb-refused" data-testid="pb-chart-cost-empty">
                                No model reported its dollars completely, so there is no measured series to
                                draw. A <span class="font-mono">zero-unverified</span> cost is excluded here
                                rather than drawn as a bar of height zero.
                            </p>
                        }
                        <p class="pb-note">
                            Token totals for the same cohort are in the command-phase table below. A
                            tokens-times-rate-card dollar never appears on this card, in this series or in
                            any total it feeds.
                        </p>
                    </CardContent>
                </Card>
            </div>

            @* ---------------------------------------------------------------------- TABLES *@
            <div class="tflens-stack" data-testid="pb-effort-tables">

                <Card>
                    <CardHeader>
                        <div class="flex flex-wrap items-start justify-between gap-2">
                            <span class="flex min-w-0 flex-col gap-1">
                                <CardTitle Class="text-base">Tokens by command phase</CardTitle>
                                <CardDescription>
                                    The five legs, per command phase — the text twin of the stacked bars above
                                </CardDescription>
                            </span>
                            <Badge Variant="BadgeVariant.Outline">@PhaseCommandGroup.DimensionKey</Badge>
                        </div>
                    </CardHeader>
                    <CardContent Class="pt-0">
                        <div class="pb-table-scroll">
                            @* TR-009 — ShowPagination="false" hides the pager but still truncates to
                               InitialPageSize, so the page size has to cover every row. *@
                            <DataTable TData="PhaseCommandGroup"
                                       Data="@vReport.CommandPhases"
                                       ShowToolbar="false"
                                       ShowPagination="false"
                                       InitialPageSize="200"
                                       AriaLabel="Tokens by command phase"
                                       data-testid="pb-effort-command-phases">
                                <Columns>
                                    <DataTableColumn TData="PhaseCommandGroup" TValue="string"
                                                     Property="@(aRow => aRow.CommandPhase)"
                                                     Header="@PhaseCommandGroup.DimensionLabel">
                                        <CellTemplate Context="vRow">
                                            <span class="font-mono">@vRow.CommandPhase</span>
                                        </CellTemplate>
                                    </DataTableColumn>
                                    <DataTableColumn TData="PhaseCommandGroup" TValue="int"
                                                     Property="@(aRow => aRow.Executions)"
                                                     Header="Executions" CellClass="text-right" />
                                    <DataTableColumn TData="PhaseCommandGroup" TValue="string"
                                                     Property="@(aRow => aRow.ElapsedMsMedian.Value.Display())"
                                                     Header="Median elapsed" CellClass="text-right">
                                        <CellTemplate Context="vRow">
                                            <PhaseValueText Value="@vRow.ElapsedMsMedian.Value"
                                                            MeasuredText="@DurationOf(vRow.ElapsedMsMedian.Value)"
                                                            TestId="@($"pb-phase-elapsed-{vRow.CommandPhase}")" />
                                        </CellTemplate>
                                    </DataTableColumn>
                                    <DataTableColumn TData="PhaseCommandGroup" TValue="string"
                                                     Property="@(aRow => aRow.Tokens.Input.Display())"
                                                     Header="Input" CellClass="text-right">
                                        <CellTemplate Context="vRow">
                                            <PhaseValueText Value="@vRow.Tokens.Input" />
                                        </CellTemplate>
                                    </DataTableColumn>
                                    <DataTableColumn TData="PhaseCommandGroup" TValue="string"
                                                     Property="@(aRow => aRow.Tokens.CacheRead.Display())"
                                                     Header="Cache read" CellClass="text-right">
                                        <CellTemplate Context="vRow">
                                            <PhaseValueText Value="@vRow.Tokens.CacheRead" />
                                        </CellTemplate>
                                    </DataTableColumn>
                                    <DataTableColumn TData="PhaseCommandGroup" TValue="string"
                                                     Property="@(aRow => aRow.Tokens.CacheWrite.Display())"
                                                     Header="Cache write" CellClass="text-right">
                                        <CellTemplate Context="vRow">
                                            <PhaseValueText Value="@vRow.Tokens.CacheWrite" />
                                        </CellTemplate>
                                    </DataTableColumn>
                                    <DataTableColumn TData="PhaseCommandGroup" TValue="string"
                                                     Property="@(aRow => aRow.Tokens.Output.Display())"
                                                     Header="Output" CellClass="text-right">
                                        <CellTemplate Context="vRow">
                                            <PhaseValueText Value="@vRow.Tokens.Output" />
                                        </CellTemplate>
                                    </DataTableColumn>
                                    <DataTableColumn TData="PhaseCommandGroup" TValue="string"
                                                     Property="@(aRow => aRow.Tokens.Reasoning.Display())"
                                                     Header="Reasoning" CellClass="text-right">
                                        <CellTemplate Context="vRow">
                                            <PhaseValueText Value="@vRow.Tokens.Reasoning" />
                                        </CellTemplate>
                                    </DataTableColumn>
                                </Columns>
                            </DataTable>
                        </div>
                        <p class="pb-note">
                            The dimension is the command phase — the measured slash command. One command
                            can contain several conceptual lifecycle stages, and its window is never split
                            between them by token proportion, because that would be arithmetic dressed as
                            measurement.
                        </p>
                    </CardContent>
                </Card>

                <Card>
                    <CardHeader>
                        <div class="flex flex-wrap items-start justify-between gap-2">
                            <span class="flex min-w-0 flex-col gap-1">
                                <CardTitle Class="text-base">Active vs wall clock</CardTitle>
                                <CardDescription>Eligible executions only — never a productivity ratio</CardDescription>
                            </span>
                            <Badge Variant="BadgeVariant.Outline" data-testid="pb-active-eligible">
                                @ActiveEligibleText
                            </Badge>
                        </div>
                    </CardHeader>
                    <CardContent Class="pt-0">
                        <div class="pb-table-scroll">
                            <DataTable TData="ActiveRow"
                                       Data="@ActiveRows"
                                       ShowToolbar="false"
                                       ShowPagination="false"
                                       InitialPageSize="200"
                                       AriaLabel="Active time against wall clock"
                                       data-testid="pb-effort-active-table">
                                <Columns>
                                    <DataTableColumn TData="ActiveRow" TValue="string"
                                                     Property="@(aRow => aRow.CommandPhase)"
                                                     Header="@PhaseCommandGroup.DimensionLabel">
                                        <CellTemplate Context="vRow">
                                            <span class="font-mono">@vRow.CommandPhase</span>
                                        </CellTemplate>
                                    </DataTableColumn>
                                    <DataTableColumn TData="ActiveRow" TValue="string"
                                                     Property="@(aRow => aRow.Wall.Display())"
                                                     Header="Median wall" CellClass="text-right">
                                        <CellTemplate Context="vRow">
                                            <PhaseValueText Value="@vRow.Wall"
                                                            TestId="@($"pb-active-wall-{vRow.CommandPhase}")" />
                                        </CellTemplate>
                                    </DataTableColumn>
                                    <DataTableColumn TData="ActiveRow" TValue="string"
                                                     Property="@(aRow => aRow.ActiveText)"
                                                     Header="Median active" CellClass="text-right">
                                        <CellTemplate Context="vRow">
                                            @if (vRow.Active is { } vActive)
                                            {
                                                <PhaseValueText Value="@vActive"
                                                                TestId="@($"pb-active-active-{vRow.CommandPhase}")" />
                                            }
                                            else
                                            {
                                                @* BRD-156 — partial coverage is an explicit lower bound and
                                                   unavailable coverage is no figure at all. Neither is ever
                                                   completed with an estimate. *@
                                                <span class="pb-refused pb-lower-bound"
                                                      data-testid="@($"pb-active-active-{vRow.CommandPhase}")">@vRow.ActiveText</span>
                                            }
                                        </CellTemplate>
                                    </DataTableColumn>
                                    <DataTableColumn TData="ActiveRow" TValue="string"
                                                     Property="@(aRow => aRow.ShareText)"
                                                     Header="Active share">
                                        <CellTemplate Context="vRow">
                                            @if (vRow.Share is { } vShare)
                                            {
                                                <span class="pb-share">
                                                    <span class="pb-share-track">
                                                        <span class="pb-share-fill" style="@PercentCss(vShare)"></span>
                                                    </span>
                                                    <span class="pb-share-pct">@vRow.ShareText</span>
                                                </span>
                                            }
                                            else
                                            {
                                                <span class="pb-refused font-mono">@vRow.ShareText</span>
                                            }
                                        </CellTemplate>
                                    </DataTableColumn>
                                </Columns>
                            </DataTable>
                        </div>
                        <p class="pb-note">
                            <span class="font-mono">partial</span> renders as an explicit lower bound;
                            <span class="font-mono">unavailable</span> renders as no figure at all. Neither
                            is ever completed with an estimate, and neither joins a comparison. A cohort
                            below @MetricsConstants.MinN records refuses to be a number.
                        </p>
                    </CardContent>
                </Card>

                <Card>
                    <CardHeader>
                        <div class="flex flex-wrap items-start justify-between gap-2">
                            <span class="flex min-w-0 flex-col gap-1">
                                <CardTitle Class="text-base">Model mix</CardTitle>
                                <CardDescription>
                                    Token share and turn share are two different measures
                                </CardDescription>
                            </span>
                            <Badge Variant="BadgeVariant.Outline">from&nbsp;<span class="font-mono">phase_model_usage</span></Badge>
                        </div>
                    </CardHeader>
                    <CardContent Class="pt-0">
                        <div class="pb-table-scroll">
                            <DataTable TData="ModelRow"
                                       Data="@ModelRows"
                                       ShowToolbar="false"
                                       ShowPagination="false"
                                       InitialPageSize="200"
                                       AriaLabel="Model mix"
                                       data-testid="pb-effort-model-mix">
                                <Columns>
                                    <DataTableColumn TData="ModelRow" TValue="string"
                                                     Property="@(aRow => aRow.Model)" Header="Model">
                                        <CellTemplate Context="vRow">
                                            <span class="font-mono">@vRow.Model</span>
                                        </CellTemplate>
                                    </DataTableColumn>
                                    <DataTableColumn TData="ModelRow" TValue="string"
                                                     Property="@(aRow => aRow.TokenShareText)" Header="Token share">
                                        <CellTemplate Context="vRow">
                                            <span class="pb-share">
                                                <span class="pb-share-track">
                                                    <span class="pb-share-fill" style="@PercentCss(vRow.TokenShare)"></span>
                                                </span>
                                                <span class="pb-share-pct"
                                                      data-testid="@($"pb-model-tokens-{vRow.Model}")">@vRow.TokenShareText</span>
                                            </span>
                                        </CellTemplate>
                                    </DataTableColumn>
                                    <DataTableColumn TData="ModelRow" TValue="string"
                                                     Property="@(aRow => aRow.TurnShareText)" Header="Turn share">
                                        <CellTemplate Context="vRow">
                                            <span class="pb-share">
                                                <span class="pb-share-track">
                                                    <span class="pb-share-fill pb-share-turns"
                                                          style="@PercentCss(vRow.TurnShare)"></span>
                                                </span>
                                                <span class="pb-share-pct">@vRow.TurnShareText</span>
                                            </span>
                                        </CellTemplate>
                                    </DataTableColumn>
                                    <DataTableColumn TData="ModelRow" TValue="int"
                                                     Property="@(aRow => aRow.Executions)"
                                                     Header="Executions" CellClass="text-right" />
                                    <DataTableColumn TData="ModelRow" TValue="string"
                                                     Property="@(aRow => aRow.CostText)"
                                                     Header="Measured cost" CellClass="text-right">
                                        <CellTemplate Context="vRow">
                                            <span class="@(vRow.HasCost ? "tabular-nums" : "pb-refused")">@vRow.CostText</span>
                                        </CellTemplate>
                                    </DataTableColumn>
                                </Columns>
                            </DataTable>
                        </div>
                        <p class="pb-note">
                            Executions can sum past the phase count because a mixed-model execution is
                            counted under every model that ran in it, never under its dominant label alone.
                            A model filter matches any member of <span class="font-mono">models[]</span>.
                            This describes what ran; it is not a causal claim about which model is better.
                        </p>
                    </CardContent>
                </Card>
            </div>

            @* -------------------------------------------------------------- EXECUTION TABLE *@
            <div class="pb-section-head">
                <h3 class="pb-h3">Executions</h3>
                <span class="text-sm text-muted-foreground">
                    One row per phase execution, upserted on
                    <span class="font-mono">(user, repo, phase_execution_id)</span> — re-import is expected.
                    The whole-task total is @PlaybookPhaseVocabulary.Unavailable: the producer emits no
                    trustworthy cross-command task id, and a reused session id is not a cohort.
                </span>
            </div>

            <Card data-testid="pb-effort-executions">
                <CardHeader>
                    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-start justify-between gap-2">
                        <span class="flex min-w-0 flex-col gap-1">
                            <CardTitle Class="text-base">Phase executions</CardTitle>
                            <CardDescription>@ExecutionsCaption</CardDescription>
                        </span>
                        <Badge Variant="BadgeVariant.Outline" data-testid="pb-executions-count">
                            @FilteredExecutions.Count of @vReport.Executions.Count
                        </Badge>
                    </div>
                </CardHeader>
                <CardContent Class="pt-0">
                    @if (FilteredExecutions.Count == 0)
                    {
                        <Alert Variant="AlertVariant.Warning" data-testid="pb-effort-no-eligible">
                            <LucideIcon Name="filter" Size="16" />
                            <AlertTitle>Every row is filtered out</AlertTitle>
                            <AlertDescription>
                                @vReport.Executions.Count stored executions, none matching the current
                                filters. The count and the reason are shown rather than an aggregate
                                printed from zero rows.
                            </AlertDescription>
                        </Alert>
                    }
                    else
                    {
                        <div class="pb-table-scroll">
                            <DataTable TData="PbExecutionRow"
                                       Data="@FilteredExecutions"
                                       ShowToolbar="false"
                                       ShowPagination="true"
                                       InitialPageSize="25"
                                       AriaLabel="Phase executions"
                                       data-testid="pb-executions-table">
                                <Columns>
                                    <DataTableColumn TData="PbExecutionRow" TValue="string"
                                                     Property="@(aRow => aRow.CommandPhase)"
                                                     Header="@PhaseCommandGroup.DimensionLabel">
                                        <CellTemplate Context="vRow">
                                            <Button Variant="ButtonVariant.Ghost"
                                                    Size="ButtonSize.Small"
                                                    Class="pb-row-trigger"
                                                    OnClick="@(() => SelectExecution(vRow.Id))"
                                                    data-testid="@($"pb-execution-open-{vRow.Id}")">
                                                <LucideIcon Name="@(IsSelected(vRow.Id) ? "chevron-down" : "chevron-right")"
                                                            Size="14" />
                                                <span class="font-mono">@vRow.CommandPhase</span>
                                            </Button>
                                        </CellTemplate>
                                    </DataTableColumn>
                                    <DataTableColumn TData="PbExecutionRow" TValue="string"
                                                     Property="@(aRow => aRow.StartedText)" Header="Started (UTC)">
                                        <CellTemplate Context="vRow">
                                            <span class="pb-small pb-when">@vRow.StartedText</span>
                                        </CellTemplate>
                                    </DataTableColumn>
                                    <DataTableColumn TData="PbExecutionRow" TValue="string"
                                                     Property="@(aRow => aRow.View.ElapsedMs.Display())"
                                                     Header="Elapsed" CellClass="text-right">
                                        <CellTemplate Context="vRow">
                                            <PhaseValueText Value="@vRow.View.ElapsedMs"
                                                            MeasuredText="@DurationOf(vRow.View.ElapsedMs)"
                                                            TestId="@($"pb-execution-elapsed-{vRow.Id}")" />
                                        </CellTemplate>
                                    </DataTableColumn>
                                    <DataTableColumn TData="PbExecutionRow" TValue="string"
                                                     Property="@(aRow => aRow.View.ObservedActiveMs.Display())"
                                                     Header="Active" CellClass="text-right">
                                        <CellTemplate Context="vRow">
                                            <PhaseValueText Value="@vRow.View.ObservedActiveMs"
                                                            MeasuredText="@ActiveTextOf(vRow.View)" />
                                        </CellTemplate>
                                    </DataTableColumn>
                                    <DataTableColumn TData="PbExecutionRow" TValue="string"
                                                     Property="@(aRow => aRow.OutTokensText)"
                                                     Header="Out tokens" CellClass="text-right">
                                        <CellTemplate Context="vRow">
                                            <span class="@(vRow.View.TokensOutput is null ? "pb-refused" : "tabular-nums")">
                                                @vRow.OutTokensText
                                            </span>
                                        </CellTemplate>
                                    </DataTableColumn>
                                    <DataTableColumn TData="PbExecutionRow" TValue="string"
                                                     Property="@(aRow => aRow.View.Cost.Display())"
                                                     Header="Cost" CellClass="text-right">
                                        <CellTemplate Context="vRow">
                                            @* BRD-160 — a zero-unverified cost shows its status, never $0
                                               as spend and never "free". *@
                                            <span class="@(vRow.View.Cost.IsMeasured ? "tabular-nums" : "pb-refused")"
                                                  title="@vRow.View.Cost.Caveat"
                                                  data-testid="@($"pb-execution-cost-{vRow.Id}")">@CostTextOf(vRow.View.Cost)</span>
                                        </CellTemplate>
                                    </DataTableColumn>
                                    <DataTableColumn TData="PbExecutionRow" TValue="string"
                                                     Property="@(aRow => aRow.View.Fanout.Display())"
                                                     Header="Sub-agents" CellClass="text-right">
                                        <CellTemplate Context="vRow">
                                            <span class="@(vRow.View.Fanout.Spawned is null ? "pb-refused" : "tabular-nums")">
                                                @vRow.View.Fanout.Display()
                                            </span>
                                        </CellTemplate>
                                    </DataTableColumn>
                                    <DataTableColumn TData="PbExecutionRow" TValue="string"
                                                     Property="@(aRow => aRow.QualityText)" Header="Data quality">
                                        <CellTemplate Context="vRow">
                                            <span class="pb-quality">
                                                <Badge Variant="@vRow.QualityVariant"
                                                       data-testid="@($"pb-execution-quality-{vRow.Id}")">@vRow.QualityText</Badge>
                                                @if (vRow.QualityDetail is { } vDetail)
                                                {
                                                    @* The reason codes are the row's own, and they are
                                                       shown rather than hidden: a quarantined row must
                                                       never read as work that never happened. *@
                                                    <span class="pb-quality-detail font-mono">@vDetail</span>
                                                }
                                            </span>
                                        </CellTemplate>
                                    </DataTableColumn>
                                </Columns>
                            </DataTable>
                        </div>

                        @if (SelectedExecution is { } vSelected)
                        {
                            <Collapsible @bind-Open="objIsDetailOpen" data-testid="pb-execution-detail">
                                <div class="pb-detail">
                                    <CollapsibleTrigger>
                                        <span class="pb-detail-trigger">
                                            <LucideIcon Name="chevron-down" Size="16" />
                                            <span class="font-mono">@(vSelected.CommandPhase ?? PlaybookPhaseVocabulary.Unavailable)</span>
                                            <span class="pb-small">— @StartedText(vSelected)</span>
                                            <span class="pb-filters-spacer"></span>
                                            <Badge Variant="BadgeVariant.Secondary">expanded</Badge>
                                        </span>
                                    </CollapsibleTrigger>
                                    <CollapsibleContent>
                                        <div class="pb-panels">

                                            @* Panel 1 — per-model usage and active time. *@
                                            <div class="pb-panel" data-testid="pb-detail-models">
                                                <div class="pb-panel-label">Per-model usage and active time</div>
                                                <div class="pb-chips">
                                                    @if (vSelected.Models.Count == 0)
                                                    {
                                                        <span class="pb-refused">
                                                            No per-model row was stored for this execution.
                                                        </span>
                                                    }
                                                    else
                                                    {
                                                        @foreach (var vModel in vSelected.Models)
                                                        {
                                                            <Badge Variant="BadgeVariant.Outline">
                                                                <span class="font-mono">@vModel</span>
                                                            </Badge>
                                                        }
                                                    }
                                                </div>
                                                <table class="pb-kv">
                                                    <tbody>
                                                        @foreach (var vRow in ModelPanelRows(vSelected))
                                                        {
                                                            <tr>
                                                                <td>@vRow.Label</td>
                                                                <td class="pb-kv-value">@vRow.Text</td>
                                                            </tr>
                                                        }
                                                    </tbody>
                                                </table>
                                                <p class="pb-note">
                                                    Invariants checked at ingest:
                                                    <span class="font-mono">tokens_in = input + cache_read + cache_write</span>
                                                    and <span class="font-mono">tokens_out = output + reasoning</span>.
                                                    A row failing either is quarantined with its reason and never
                                                    repaired. The report publishes per-model usage as an
                                                    aggregate over the whole cohort — see Model mix above —
                                                    and not as a split of one execution's window, because
                                                    apportioning one window across the models that ran in it
                                                    would be a figure the transcripts do not support.
                                                </p>
                                            </div>

                                            @* Panel 2 — the recursive session tree (BRD-159). *@
                                            <div class="pb-panel" data-testid="pb-detail-subagents">
                                                <div class="pb-panel-label">
                                                    Sub-agent tree — contributors / spawned
                                                    <span class="font-mono">@vSelected.Fanout.Display()</span>
                                                </div>
                                                @if (vSelected.Fanout.Tree.Count == 0)
                                                {
                                                    <p class="pb-refused">
                                                        No child session was stored for this execution.
                                                        @(vSelected.Fanout.Spawned is null
                                                            ? "The window's scope never read the sub-agent transcripts, so it reported nothing rather than none."
                                                            : string.Empty)
                                                    </p>
                                                }
                                                else
                                                {
                                                    <table class="pb-tree">
                                                        <thead>
                                                            <tr>
                                                                <th>Session</th>
                                                                <th>Agent type</th>
                                                                <th class="pb-right">Out tokens</th>
                                                                <th class="pb-right">Provider cost</th>
                                                            </tr>
                                                        </thead>
                                                        <tbody>
                                                            @foreach (var vNode in Flatten(vSelected.Fanout.Tree, 0))
                                                            {
                                                                <tr class="@(vNode.Node.TokensOut is > 0 ? null : "pb-muted-row")">
                                                                    <td style="@IndentCss(vNode.Depth)">
                                                                        <span class="font-mono">@Marker(vNode.Depth)@vNode.Node.SessionId</span>
                                                                    </td>
                                                                    <td class="pb-small">
                                                                        <span class="@(IsNamed(vNode.Node.AgentDisplay) ? "font-mono" : "pb-refused")">
                                                                            @vNode.Node.AgentDisplay
                                                                        </span>
                                                                    </td>
                                                                    <td class="pb-right">
                                                                        <span class="@(vNode.Node.TokensOut is null ? "pb-refused" : "tabular-nums")">
                                                                            @NullableTokenText(vNode.Node.TokensOut)
                                                                        </span>
                                                                    </td>
                                                                    <td class="pb-right">
                                                                        <span class="@(vNode.Node.CostUsd is null ? "pb-refused" : "tabular-nums")">
                                                                            @DollarText(vNode.Node.CostUsd)
                                                                        </span>
                                                                    </td>
                                                                </tr>
                                                            }
                                                        </tbody>
                                                    </table>
                                                }
                                                <p class="pb-note">
                                                    Child usage is already inside the phase totals and is never
                                                    summed onto them again; a grandchild renders beneath its
                                                    parent and counts exactly once. The
                                                    <span class="font-mono">spawned − contributors</span> gap is a
                                                    @vSelected.Fanout.NonContributingLabel, not an inferred
                                                    failure. An absent child agent type shows
                                                    <span class="font-mono">@PlaybookPhaseVocabulary.Unavailable</span>;
                                                    it is never guessed as
                                                    <span class="font-mono">"unknown"</span> from a title or a
                                                    model name. Dollars here are the provider's own per-session
                                                    figures; no dollar is apportioned across children.
                                                </p>
                                            </div>

                                            @* Panel 3 — the five data-quality explanations. *@
                                            <div class="pb-panel" data-testid="pb-detail-quality">
                                                <div class="pb-panel-label">Data quality</div>
                                                <table class="pb-kv">
                                                    <tbody>
                                                        @foreach (var vRow in QualityPanelRows(vSelected))
                                                        {
                                                            <tr>
                                                                <td>@vRow.Label</td>
                                                                <td class="pb-kv-value">
                                                                    <span class="@(vRow.IsRefused ? "pb-refused" : null)">@vRow.Text</span>
                                                                </td>
                                                            </tr>
                                                        }
                                                    </tbody>
                                                </table>
                                                @if (vSelected.QuarantineReasons.Count > 0)
                                                {
                                                    <ul class="pb-reasons" data-testid="pb-detail-quarantine">
                                                        @foreach (var vReason in vSelected.QuarantineReasons)
                                                        {
                                                            <li>
                                                                <span class="font-mono">@vReason.Code</span> —
                                                                @vReason.Explanation
                                                            </li>
                                                        }
                                                    </ul>
                                                }
                                            </div>
                                        </div>
                                    </CollapsibleContent>
                                </div>
                            </Collapsible>
                        }
                    }
                </CardContent>
            </Card>

            @* BRD-163 — the standing statement, rendered on the supported state too, because a reader
               looking at OpenCode figures must not read them as covering every harness. *@
            <div class="pb-section-head">
                <h3 class="pb-h3">Harnesses with no normalized producer</h3>
            </div>
            <Alert Variant="AlertVariant.Warning" AccentBorder="true" data-testid="pb-effort-unsupported">
                <LucideIcon Name="triangle-alert" Size="18" />
                <AlertTitle>
                    @PlaybookPhaseVocabulary.UnsupportedHarnessMessage —
                    <span class="font-mono">@UnsupportedHarnessList</span>
                </AlertTitle>
                <AlertDescription>
                    Only @NormalizedHarnessList emits the normalized schema-2 phase record, so there is
                    nothing to render for any other harness on this axis. That is a data gap, which is a
                    different fact from a harness that ran and spent nothing — it is never rendered as 0
                    and never as an empty measured figure, and none of the figures above claims to cover it.
                </AlertDescription>
            </Alert>
        }

        @* The five states, always on the page, because "nothing here" has five different causes. *@
        <Card data-testid="pb-effort-states">
            <CardHeader>
                <div class="flex flex-wrap items-start justify-between gap-2">
                    <span class="flex min-w-0 flex-col gap-1">
                        <CardTitle Class="text-base">Empty and unsupported states</CardTitle>
                        <CardDescription>
                            Five distinct conditions — each says which one it is
                        </CardDescription>
                    </span>
                    <Badge Variant="BadgeVariant.Outline" data-testid="pb-effort-state-active">@ActiveStateName</Badge>
                </div>
            </CardHeader>
            <CardContent Class="pt-0">
                <div class="pb-table-scroll">
                    <DataTable TData="StateRow"
                               Data="@StateRows"
                               ShowToolbar="false"
                               ShowPagination="false"
                               InitialPageSize="20"
                               AriaLabel="Empty and unsupported states"
                               data-testid="pb-effort-states-table">
                        <Columns>
                            <DataTableColumn TData="StateRow" TValue="string"
                                             Property="@(aRow => aRow.Name)" Header="State">
                                <CellTemplate Context="vRow">
                                    <span class="font-mono @(vRow.IsActive ? "font-semibold" : null)"
                                          data-testid="@($"pb-effort-state-{vRow.Name}")">@vRow.Name</span>
                                </CellTemplate>
                            </DataTableColumn>
                            <DataTableColumn TData="StateRow" TValue="string"
                                             Property="@(aRow => aRow.Description)" Header="What is shown">
                                <CellTemplate Context="vRow">
                                    <span class="pb-small">@vRow.Description</span>
                                </CellTemplate>
                            </DataTableColumn>
                        </Columns>
                    </DataTable>
                </div>
                <p class="pb-note">
                    Storage and filtering are UTC; only display is localized. Any comparative cohort below
                    @MetricsConstants.MinN records renders <i>insufficient data (n=…)</i>. No figure on this
                    page, in the API, in the export or in parity is grouped by
                    <span class="font-mono">actor</span>.
                </p>
            </CardContent>
        </Card>
    }
</div>

@code {
    /// <summary>What a value the producer never carried renders as — never a zero.</summary>
    private const string Dash = "—";

    /// <summary>The filter key of the repository select, which is the one filter that re-queries.</summary>
    private const string RepoFilterKey = "repository";

    /// <summary>The option key every "all …" filter option carries.</summary>
    private const string AllKey = "all";

    /// <summary>
    /// The culture every dollar on this surface is formatted in.
    /// </summary>
    /// <remarks>
    /// The engine renders with the invariant culture, whose currency sign is the placeholder glyph. The
    /// number is the engine's; only the symbol is chosen here, and it matches every other dollar in the
    /// product.
    /// </remarks>
    private static readonly CultureInfo Money = CultureInfo.GetCultureInfo("en-US");

    private PlaybookPhaseReport? objReport;
    private IReadOnlyList<RepoListItem> objRepos = [];
    private bool objIsLoaded;
    private string? objLoadError;
    private int? objLoadedUserId;
    private string? objSelectedExecutionId;
    private bool objIsDetailOpen = true;
    private readonly Dictionary<string, string> objFilters = new(StringComparer.Ordinal);

    /// <summary>The signed-in user whose phase figures are shown; nothing loads without one (ADR-013).</summary>
    [Parameter]
    [EditorRequired]
    public int? UserId { get; set; }

    /// <summary>The report the surface renders, exposed so the page can tell whether a read failed.</summary>
    public PlaybookPhaseReport? Report => objReport;

    /// <summary>The harnesses that do emit the normalized schema-2 record, as a sentence fragment.</summary>
    private static string NormalizedHarnessList =>
        string.Join(", ", PlaybookPhaseAdapter.NormalizedHarnesses);

    /// <summary>The harnesses TfLens detects that have no normalized phase producer.</summary>
    /// <remarks>
    /// Named from the harness vocabulary rather than from the connected repositories, because the
    /// statement is standing: it is true whether or not this user happens to have such a repository.
    /// </remarks>
    private static string UnsupportedHarnessList =>
        string.Join(", ", new[] { "claude-code", "codex" });

    /// <summary>The harness the report was judged on, or the word for "none was detected".</summary>
    private string HarnessName =>
        objRepos.Count == 0 ? PlaybookPhaseVocabulary.Unavailable : "claude-code";

    /// <summary>The sentence under the no-bundle empty state.</summary>
    private static string NoBundleDescription =>
        "The harness emits the normalized record, but no phase-metric bundle has been imported for it "
        + "yet. Import one through Repos → Add source → Import metric files: the exporter's input event "
        + "file is transient and rotates by design, so TfLens never fetches it.";

    /// <summary>What the filters narrow, stated plainly rather than left for a reader to infer.</summary>
    private static string FilterScopeNote =>
        "The repository select re-queries the engine, so every figure changes with it. The other filters "
        + "narrow the execution table only: the summary figures are the engine's four nested cohorts with "
        + "their own exclusion counts, and re-deriving them from a filtered row set here would be a second "
        + "implementation of the rules that keep an unmeasured value from becoming a zero. Tier and tokens "
        + "scope are not carried on the published execution view, so those two select nothing yet.";

    /// <summary>The caption beneath the completed-phases tile.</summary>
    private string CompletedCaption =>
        objReport is null
            ? string.Empty
            : $"{objReport.Quality.Completed} of {objReport.Quality.Records} executions eligible · "
              + $"{objReport.Quality.Incomplete} windows ended at eof and carry no elapsed time";

    /// <summary>The caption beneath the token tile — the five legs, each over the same cohort.</summary>
    private string TokenCaption
    {
        get
        {
            if (objReport is null)
            {
                return string.Empty;
            }

            var vTokens = objReport.Tokens;

            return $"output shown · input {vTokens.Input.Display()} · cache read {vTokens.CacheRead.Display()}"
                   + $" · cache write {vTokens.CacheWrite.Display()} · reasoning {vTokens.Reasoning.Display()}"
                   + $" · {vTokens.N} of {objReport.Quality.Records} eligible (valid + token_status complete)";
        }
    }

    /// <summary>The measured total, or the engine's own refusal — never a zero standing in for one.</summary>
    private string MeasuredCostText =>
        objReport?.MeasuredCostUsd.Usd is { } vUsd
            ? vUsd.ToString("C4", Money)
